  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "A body of density $\\rho^{\\prime}$ is dropped from rest at a height h into a lake of density $\\rho$ where $\\rho>\\rho^{\\prime}$ neglecting all dissipative forces, calculate the maximum depth to which the body sinks before returning to float on the surface:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "KNBWe",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\mathrm{h}}{\\rho-\\rho^{\\prime}}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "QdJJM",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\mathrm{h} \\rho^{\\prime}}{\\rho}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "uvZe5",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\mathrm{h} \\rho^{\\prime}}{\\rho-\\rho^{\\prime}}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "z4uk1",
      "text": "$\\frac{h \\rho}{\\rho-\\rho^{\\prime}}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The effective acceleration of the body\r\n\r\n$\\mathrm{g}^{\\prime}=\\left(1-\\frac{\\rho}{\\rho^{\\prime}}\\right) \\mathrm{g}$\r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/oEm_LCHuM0OzQE1UaLX4fufNHlvQQinJ9ebj1CpNf08.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\r\n\r\nNow, the depth to which the body sinks\r\n\r\n$\\mathrm{h}^{\\prime}=\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{u}^{2}}{2 \\mathrm{~g}^{\\prime}}\\right)=\\frac{2 \\mathrm{gh}}{2 \\mathrm{~g}^{\\prime}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{gh}}{\\mathrm{g}^{\\prime}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{h} \\times \\rho^{\\prime}}{\\rho-\\rho^{\\prime}}$",
    "image": null
  },
